bna|n|A very small and close apartment, as in a prison or in a monastery or convent; the hut of a hermit. ; A small religious house attached to a monastery or convent. ; Any small cavity, or hollow place. ; The space between the ribs of a vaulted roof. ; Same as Cella. ; A jar of vessel, or a division of a compound vessel, for holding the exciting fluid of a battery. ; One of the minute elementary structures, of which the greater part of the various tissues and organs of animals and plants are composed.	n:17hv,74,8~17hv,74,8	N:1jn1,117,13;1jmz,101,25;hix,67,2;7xn,61,1~1jmz,101,25;1jn1,117,13;hix,67,2;7xn,61,1
